Skip the whole realtime mode picker for a macroblock the active map excludes.

libvpx honours VP8E_SET_ACTIVEMAP already, but the check lives deep inside
evaluate_inter_mode(), which vp8_pick_inter_mode() only reaches after running
get_predictor_pointers(), the dot-artifact check (SAD over Y and both chroma
planes), the skin-map lookup, get_reference_search_order(),
vp8_find_near_mvs_bias() and part of the mode loop -- all for a macroblock the
caller has already said is not to be coded.

On hardware where VP8 is the bottleneck that prologue *is* the frame rate.
Measured on IRIX 6.5.22m / R5000 under IRIS, three interleaved rounds of a frame
whose active map selects nothing at all (`perfprobe floor`):

               stock          patched
   160x128      23/30/24 ms   21/18/20 ms
   320x256      51/50/51 ms   39/34/37 ms
   640x512     166/172/191 ms 95/91/94 ms     1.9x
  1280x1024    753/708/712 ms 309/348/340 ms  2.2x

That is the floor under every frame no matter how little changed, and on a
remote desktop almost nothing changes: at 640x512 it took the ceiling from 5.8
to 10.5 frames per second.

The answer for an excluded macroblock is a definition rather than a search
result -- nothing here moved, so code it as ZEROMV against LAST and skip it.
That is where the existing late exit lands anyway: it sets x->skip, and the mode
loop then takes its `|| x->skip` branch and breaks. So this changes when the
decision is made, not what it is.

Placed in vp8cx_encode_inter_macroblock() rather than inside the picker so that
it covers the RD path as well, and so the work that follows a skip -- building
the inter predictors, setting mb_skip_coeff, vp8_fix_contexts -- is done here
exactly as that function does it for any other skipped macroblock.

Verified on the target, not just built: a 100-second session against a moving
desktop, every frame decoded by the peer, and the decoded picture compared
against a fresh capture of the same screen -- mean absolute difference 2.40 of
255, and every large difference inside the one region (an xclock) that was still
moving. A wrongly-skipped macroblock would show up there as a block of large
differences and nowhere else.

--- a/vp8/encoder/encodeframe.c
+++ b/vp8/encoder/encodeframe.c
@@ -1122,6 +1122,59 @@
 
   x->skip = 0;
 
+  /* A macroblock the caller has excluded needs no search at all.
+   *
+   * libvpx honours the active map already, but only inside
+   * evaluate_inter_mode() -- by which point vp8_pick_inter_mode() has run
+   * get_predictor_pointers(), the dot-artifact check (SAD over Y and both
+   * chroma planes), the skin-map lookup, get_reference_search_order(),
+   * vp8_find_near_mvs_bias() and part of the mode loop, all to decide
+   * something the caller stated.
+   *
+   * On hardware where VP8 is the bottleneck that prologue is the frame rate.
+   * On IRIX 6.5 / R5000 at 640x512, a frame whose map selects *nothing* still
+   * costs 173 ms -- 0.135 ms per excluded macroblock, 1280 times -- and that is
+   * the floor under every frame however little changed. On a remote desktop,
+   * almost nothing changes.
+   *
+   * The answer here is a definition rather than a search result: nothing moved,
+   * so code it as ZEROMV against LAST and skip it. That is where the existing
+   * late exit lands anyway (it sets x->skip, the mode loop takes its `||
+   * x->skip` branch and breaks), so this changes when the decision is made and
+   * not what it is. Everything below -- the inter predictors, mb_skip_coeff,
+   * vp8_fix_contexts -- then runs as it does for any other skipped macroblock.
+   */
+  if (cpi->active_map_enabled && x->active_ptr[0] == 0) {
+    MB_MODE_INFO *mbmi = &xd->mode_info_context->mbmi;
+    mbmi->mode = ZEROMV;
+    mbmi->ref_frame = LAST_FRAME;
+    mbmi->mv.as_int = 0;
+    mbmi->uv_mode = DC_PRED;
+    mbmi->partitioning = 0;
+    mbmi->need_to_clamp_mvs = 0;
+    x->skip = 1;
+    x->mbs_tested_so_far++;
+    x->count_mb_ref_frame_usage[LAST_FRAME]++;
+
+    xd->pre.y_buffer =
+        cpi->common.yv12_fb[cpi->common.lst_fb_idx].y_buffer + recon_yoffset;
+    xd->pre.u_buffer =
+        cpi->common.yv12_fb[cpi->common.lst_fb_idx].u_buffer + recon_uvoffset;
+    xd->pre.v_buffer =
+        cpi->common.yv12_fb[cpi->common.lst_fb_idx].v_buffer + recon_uvoffset;
+    vp8_build_inter16x16_predictors_mb(xd, xd->dst.y_buffer, xd->dst.u_buffer,
+                                       xd->dst.v_buffer, xd->dst.y_stride,
+                                       xd->dst.uv_stride);
+    mbmi->mb_skip_coeff = 1;
+    if (cpi->common.mb_no_coeff_skip) {
+      x->skip_true_count++;
+      vp8_fix_contexts(xd);
+    } else {
+      vp8_stuff_mb(cpi, x, t);
+    }
+    return 0;
+  }
+
   if (xd->segmentation_enabled) {
     x->encode_breakout =
         cpi->segment_encode_breakout[xd->mode_info_context->mbmi.segment_id];
